/></highlight
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20251029134150+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="fd01c7c7-27d8-42e3-93d8-7edd286fcf30" date="D:20251029134223+10'00'" name="4a66857c-9001-428e-a471-c2132a170d76" icon="Comment" page="8" rect="297.212000,464.822000,321.212000,488.822000" subject="Sticky Note" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14b: there was limited practical reflections on the outcomes of the study</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="8" rect="595.276000,396.822000,779.276000,488.822000"
/></text
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20251029134226+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="fd01c7c7-27d8-42e3-93d8-7edd286fcf30" date="D:20251029134226+10'00'" name="e86c1130-f1b6-4380-971b-f1ee821d3d38" icon="Comment" page="8" rect="297.212000,464.822000,321.212000,488.822000" subject="Sticky Note" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>The current study sought to understand the perspectives of&#xD;athletes, coaches, and support staff to explore the importance&#xD;of paddling to surfing performance. We found that&#xD;despite the varied roles and experiences of the participants,&#xD;nearly all the participants reported that paddling was an&#xD;important component of surfing performance and that this&#xD;is often overlooked. Several key themes emerged that&#xD;were discussed through an ecological dynamics perspective.&#xD;These themes provided insight into potential considerations&#xD;for improving paddling performance. Future&#xD;research could focus on implementing strength, technical&#xD;and/or physiological interventions to enhance paddling performance&#xD;in women athletes. Considering the findings of&#xD;this study, enhancing the paddling ability of women&#xD;surfers may provide greater affordances with respect to&#xD;wave-riding and, in turn, accelerate skill development, as&#xD;well as elicit greater confidence and competitive advantage&#xD;during competition.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="8" rect="595.276000,396.822000,779.276000,488.822000"
/></text
